1
00:00:05,964 --> 00:00:06,924
THIS IS A WORK OF FICTION

2
00:00:07,007 --> 00:00:07,925
SCENES INVOLVING CHILDREN AND ANIMALS
WERE FILMED SAFELY ACCORDING TO GUIDELINES

3
00:00:49,383 --> 00:00:52,094
How do you like that, you fucking bastard?

4
00:00:52,177 --> 00:00:54,680
You motherfucker.

5
00:01:05,858 --> 00:01:11,864
THE AFFAIR WAS JUST THE BEGINNING

6
00:01:15,242 --> 00:01:19,413
EPISODE 4
99 MILLION WON

7
00:01:19,496 --> 00:01:21,123
No more misfortune.

8
00:01:21,748 --> 00:01:22,833
No more.

9
00:01:23,792 --> 00:01:25,043
Bless us with good fortune.

10
00:01:26,170 --> 00:01:27,296
Bless us!

11
00:01:28,297 --> 00:01:29,506
Help us secure the investment

12
00:01:31,592 --> 00:01:32,718
so we can pay off our loan.

13
00:01:33,594 --> 00:01:34,678
If we secure the investment,

14
00:01:35,679 --> 00:01:36,722
we'll buy a new car too.

15
00:01:37,973 --> 00:01:39,433
In fact, that's the first thing we'll do.

16
00:01:39,850 --> 00:01:42,519
- I can't stand the sight of it.
- Honey!

17
00:01:42,603 --> 00:01:44,396
What is this? Take a look at this!

18
00:01:45,939 --> 00:01:47,649
"What you did yesterday

19
00:01:47,733 --> 00:01:49,902
was all caught on film.

20
00:01:49,985 --> 00:01:51,486
Get me

21
00:01:51,570 --> 00:01:53,113
five hundred million won in cash

22
00:01:53,197 --> 00:01:54,239
until 5 p.m. today."

23
00:01:55,157 --> 00:01:56,366
What the hell is this?

24
00:01:56,450 --> 00:01:58,744
The video will be released
if we're even a second late.

25
00:01:58,827 --> 00:02:00,120
What do we do?

26
00:02:03,248 --> 00:02:04,249
What video?

27
00:02:04,333 --> 00:02:05,375
THE PERFECT FAMILY'S SHOCKING SECRET

28
00:02:05,459 --> 00:02:07,836
What exactly did they film?

29
00:02:07,920 --> 00:02:09,338
What the hell is this?

30
00:02:09,421 --> 00:02:10,839
I don't know.

31
00:02:11,757 --> 00:02:13,759
- How did they even get my number?
- Yesterday...

32
00:02:13,842 --> 00:02:15,636
Yesterday, we were...

33
00:02:16,178 --> 00:02:18,847
- Is this someone I know?
- What video is it?

34
00:02:18,931 --> 00:02:20,933
- This is driving me nuts.
- Hey!

35
00:02:21,016 --> 00:02:22,559
Do they really have a video of us?

36
00:02:23,519 --> 00:02:25,562
No one was there last night, right?

37
00:02:26,939 --> 00:02:28,190
Maybe they're bluffing.

38
00:02:29,399 --> 00:02:30,734
How should I know?

39
00:02:35,822 --> 00:02:38,700
I don't know what kind of video you have,

40
00:02:40,661 --> 00:02:44,164
but you can't threaten
innocent people like this.

41
00:02:47,876 --> 00:02:48,710
Shit.

42
00:02:48,794 --> 00:02:50,295
- You can't reply to that.
- Shit!

43
00:02:50,379 --> 00:02:52,798
Fucking shit!

44
00:02:52,881 --> 00:02:55,259
This is why I said
she needs to turn herself in!

45
00:02:55,342 --> 00:02:57,803
Why did you move the body
in the first place?

46
00:02:58,846 --> 00:03:00,639
You agreed to move it too!

47
00:03:01,807 --> 00:03:04,476
You're the one
who took everything out of the car

48
00:03:05,310 --> 00:03:08,814
to shove that guy inside
when he barely even fit in the car.

49
00:03:08,897 --> 00:03:10,774
Then you poured paint over everything

50
00:03:10,858 --> 00:03:13,318
and started cleaning everything up.

51
00:03:13,402 --> 00:03:16,989
I thought you were filming
one of your YouTube videos or something.

52
00:03:17,072 --> 00:03:19,157
It doesn't matter who's to blame.

53
00:03:19,241 --> 00:03:21,618
We need to stick together
if we want to survive!

54
00:03:22,536 --> 00:03:25,706
What are we going to do
about this damn text?

55
00:03:25,789 --> 00:03:27,624
Why are you yelling at me?

56
00:03:27,708 --> 00:03:31,044
We can't hand over that much cash
to this shady bastard.

57
00:03:31,128 --> 00:03:34,006
What if we hand over the money
but he uploads the video anyway?

58
00:03:34,089 --> 00:03:36,425
Then we're completely screwed!

59
00:03:37,259 --> 00:03:39,845
We have until 5 p.m. today, though.

60
00:03:39,928 --> 00:03:41,305
Do we have any other choice?

61
00:03:50,856 --> 00:03:51,940
Even if we do this,

62
00:03:53,025 --> 00:03:56,653
how are we going to get
500 million won in cash before 5 p.m.?

63
00:03:58,530 --> 00:04:00,073
First of all,

64
00:04:00,157 --> 00:04:03,452
let's scrounge up
all the cash we have in our safe.

65
00:04:05,704 --> 00:04:08,999
Do you remember
how much cash we had there?

66
00:04:10,042 --> 00:04:12,044
- At least a few hundred million, right?
- Did we?

67
00:04:12,127 --> 00:04:14,963
- Didn't we also have some gold bars?
- Yes, maybe.

68
00:04:15,255 --> 00:04:16,715
Good morning, Ye-ji.

69
00:04:24,431 --> 00:04:27,392
Hong, now that I think about it,

70
00:04:27,476 --> 00:04:29,561
I can handle this just fine.

71
00:04:29,645 --> 00:04:31,647
So don't worry too much, honey.

72
00:04:31,730 --> 00:04:33,607
What the hell?

73
00:04:33,690 --> 00:04:36,401
Do I have to make a reservation
to visit my own safe?

74
00:04:37,486 --> 00:04:39,988
I'll go to the safe by myself.

75
00:04:40,072 --> 00:04:42,699
Don't you have a meeting
with the writer of <i>Townhouse</i>?

76
00:04:42,783 --> 00:04:44,451
That's next week.

77
00:04:46,036 --> 00:04:47,746
- The left one looks nicer.
- Okay.

78
00:04:48,497 --> 00:04:51,625
What about you?
Aren't you meeting Michelle Jung today?

79
00:04:52,501 --> 00:04:55,462
Besides, I made the reservation
in my name,

80
00:04:55,546 --> 00:04:56,713
so I need to go myself.

81
00:05:00,175 --> 00:05:01,176
Hong.

82
00:05:03,428 --> 00:05:04,930
There's no cash in the safe.

83
00:05:05,973 --> 00:05:07,432
I'm sorry.

84
00:05:07,516 --> 00:05:08,350
What?

85
00:05:09,059 --> 00:05:10,644
Oh, come on.

86
00:05:11,228 --> 00:05:13,021
You know how it's been.

87
00:05:13,105 --> 00:05:15,649
Michelle suddenly
pulled out her investment

88
00:05:15,732 --> 00:05:17,526
after I'd already lined up clients

89
00:05:17,609 --> 00:05:19,403
and placed the order with the factory.

90
00:05:22,489 --> 00:05:24,825
Still, we did get
that final payment last week,

91
00:05:24,908 --> 00:05:26,243
so we can use that,

92
00:05:26,326 --> 00:05:27,536
and...

93
00:05:27,619 --> 00:05:30,247
Maybe with the gold bars in the safe,

94
00:05:30,330 --> 00:05:32,040
it might be enough.

95
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:35,752
You should've talked to me
before using that money!

96
00:05:36,461 --> 00:05:37,880
Aren't we supposed to be partners?

97
00:05:41,091 --> 00:05:43,177
Just because you're a bit more successful

98
00:05:43,260 --> 00:05:45,429
and a bit more famous than me

99
00:05:46,013 --> 00:05:48,557
doesn't mean you can
treat your husband this way!

100
00:05:48,640 --> 00:05:51,351
You always make decisions by yourself!

101
00:05:53,228 --> 00:05:54,062
Sorry.

102
00:05:55,230 --> 00:05:57,691
I'm really sorry. It was my bad.

103
00:06:00,777 --> 00:06:03,113
What are we going to do now?

104
00:06:03,906 --> 00:06:06,533
Where can we get that much money
in such a short time?

105
00:06:07,701 --> 00:06:10,495
If that video ever leaks,

106
00:06:10,579 --> 00:06:11,705
my life...

107
00:06:14,041 --> 00:06:16,919
I mean, Ye-ji's life
is going to get very difficult.

108
00:06:18,670 --> 00:06:20,464
I'll figure something out, okay?

109
00:06:22,382 --> 00:06:23,842
I'll make it up to you.

110
00:06:25,344 --> 00:06:26,178
Okay?

111
00:06:31,934 --> 00:06:35,979
If anyone asks you how you got hurt,
tell them you bumped into your bed.

112
00:06:38,065 --> 00:06:38,899
Okay.

113
00:06:44,738 --> 00:06:46,323
Just be cool.

114
00:06:48,742 --> 00:06:50,911
- Good morning.
- Morning.

115
00:06:50,994 --> 00:06:52,246
Good morning.

116
00:06:52,329 --> 00:06:54,289
You cut your bangs, Min-seo?

117
00:06:54,373 --> 00:06:56,625
It suits you so well.
Don't you agree, Ye-ji?

118
00:06:56,708 --> 00:06:58,377
Yes, I like it too,

119
00:06:58,460 --> 00:07:00,462
but Min-seo doesn't seem happy with it.

120
00:07:00,546 --> 00:07:01,880
We should go now, Ye-ji.

121
00:07:01,964 --> 00:07:03,006
Have a good day.

122
00:07:07,594 --> 00:07:09,763
She hasn't noticed anything, has she?

123
00:07:09,847 --> 00:07:11,932
I'm sure she hasn't.

124
00:07:12,015 --> 00:07:14,351
You're too good at hiding things.

125
00:07:30,993 --> 00:07:36,623
CHEONGNAM POLICE STATION

126
00:07:36,707 --> 00:07:38,125
I trust you, honey.

127
00:07:48,302 --> 00:07:50,387
- Can't you see I've been hit?
- Calm down.

128
00:07:50,470 --> 00:07:52,264
I think you're just drunk, sir.

129
00:07:52,347 --> 00:07:53,432
- If you'd just sit--
- Come on!

130
00:07:53,515 --> 00:07:55,434
- What are you talking about?
- Sir, please calm down.

131
00:07:55,517 --> 00:07:56,727
Sir.

132
00:07:56,810 --> 00:07:58,770
You can't yell like that.

133
00:07:58,854 --> 00:08:01,940
- Sit down and talk. We'll listen.
- Exactly.

134
00:08:02,024 --> 00:08:03,150
You're not listening to me!

135
00:08:03,233 --> 00:08:05,694
I said we'd listen! Just sit down first.

136
00:08:05,777 --> 00:08:09,239
What's wrong with you?
It's too early to be this drunk.

137
00:08:09,323 --> 00:08:11,658
Please wait there.
We'll get to you in time.

138
00:08:12,951 --> 00:08:15,454
What can I do for you, sir?

139
00:08:15,537 --> 00:08:16,955
Excuse me.

140
00:08:17,039 --> 00:08:18,040
Hello.

141
00:08:19,708 --> 00:08:22,878
It's just that I lost my car last night.

142
00:08:23,962 --> 00:08:25,339
I mean,

143
00:08:25,422 --> 00:08:27,508
I parked my car to go jogging for a bit

144
00:08:27,591 --> 00:08:29,593
near a creek in Yongsin-dong,
where my vacation home is.

145
00:08:29,676 --> 00:08:30,802
- Wait.
- Then--

146
00:08:31,428 --> 00:08:34,806
Are you in <i>Model House</i>, by any chance?

147
00:08:34,890 --> 00:08:36,391
He's Cha something.

148
00:08:36,475 --> 00:08:40,854
It's Cha Eun-bin, sir.

149
00:08:40,938 --> 00:08:43,148
And the show's actually <i>Townhouse</i>.

150
00:08:43,232 --> 00:08:44,399
Oh, that's right.

151
00:08:45,400 --> 00:08:46,693
This is so cool.

152
00:08:46,777 --> 00:08:48,612
My mom's a huge fan of that show.

153
00:08:48,695 --> 00:08:49,821
- Really?
- Yes.

154
00:08:49,905 --> 00:08:51,073
- Seriously?
- Yes.

155
00:08:51,156 --> 00:08:52,824
Would you like an autograph, then?

156
00:08:52,908 --> 00:08:54,034
Thank you.

157
00:08:54,117 --> 00:08:55,577
- Just one, then.
- Of course.

158
00:08:56,787 --> 00:08:58,622
- I'd like one too.
- Yes, sir.

159
00:09:00,541 --> 00:09:01,750
Hello.

160
00:09:04,127 --> 00:09:06,797
You said you lost your car
in Yongsin-dong?

161
00:09:08,298 --> 00:09:09,258
Yes.

162
00:09:10,092 --> 00:09:12,469
Then why did you come here a day late

163
00:09:12,553 --> 00:09:14,596
instead of going straight
to the station there?

164
00:09:16,557 --> 00:09:18,517
Well, it's because...

165
00:09:21,436 --> 00:09:23,522
You must've been flustered, right?

166
00:09:23,605 --> 00:09:26,567
Oh, right.
I was too flustered at the time.

167
00:09:27,150 --> 00:09:30,112
You were taking a walk in Yongsin-dong?

168
00:09:30,195 --> 00:09:32,239
You know that's a dangerous area, right?

169
00:09:32,322 --> 00:09:33,156
Sorry?

170
00:09:34,700 --> 00:09:36,910
It has the highest crime rate in the city.

171
00:09:40,664 --> 00:09:41,832
Yes, exactly.

172
00:09:42,583 --> 00:09:44,835
YONGSIN-DONG CRIMES
Just take a look at this.

173
00:09:44,918 --> 00:09:47,379
It says organized crime groups
like to frequent that area.

174
00:09:47,462 --> 00:09:50,132
So that's why the house was so cheap.

175
00:09:50,215 --> 00:09:54,178
I told you, didn't I?
I said the realtor looked shady too.

176
00:09:54,261 --> 00:09:56,680
So what happened?
What else did the police say?

177
00:09:59,433 --> 00:10:01,810
I did some method acting

178
00:10:01,894 --> 00:10:04,730
to fool them all into believing me.

179
00:10:05,439 --> 00:10:09,109
They even felt sorry for me,
worried that I had a tough night.

180
00:10:09,818 --> 00:10:12,279
I'm proud of you.
I couldn't have done that.

181
00:10:15,240 --> 00:10:16,325
Honey.

182
00:10:17,242 --> 00:10:19,620
How would you have survived without me?

183
00:10:21,330 --> 00:10:22,539
I couldn't have.

184
00:10:23,040 --> 00:10:24,833
Also, I've been thinking,

185
00:10:24,917 --> 00:10:27,169
and I think we can cover it
with the company money.

186
00:10:27,836 --> 00:10:29,254
Really?

187
00:10:29,338 --> 00:10:31,548
- Are you sure?
- Yes, for now.

188
00:10:34,760 --> 00:10:38,680
5 HOURS BEFORE THE VIDEO LEAK

189
00:10:39,056 --> 00:10:40,140
Why not?

190
00:10:41,141 --> 00:10:43,519
We use temporary advances all the time.

191
00:10:43,602 --> 00:10:45,270
You said it wasn't a problem.

192
00:10:45,354 --> 00:10:47,147
<i>I'm sure you know better than me,</i>

193
00:10:47,231 --> 00:10:50,526
<i>but there are risks of an audit,</i>
<i>and the investment rights are on the line.</i>

194
00:10:50,609 --> 00:10:52,402
<i>What if Michelle Jung</i>
<i>uses that as an excuse</i>

195
00:10:52,486 --> 00:10:54,530
<i>to pull her investment again?</i>

196
00:10:55,948 --> 00:10:57,449
Why can't I withdraw the money?

197
00:10:59,201 --> 00:11:02,079
Banks don't keep a lot of cash these days.

198
00:11:02,871 --> 00:11:04,748
Today, 300 million won is the maximum.

199
00:11:05,999 --> 00:11:10,128
You can withdraw the rest in a few days
if you make a reservation.

200
00:11:11,255 --> 00:11:12,464
Would you like to do that?

201
00:11:17,427 --> 00:11:19,388
EXECUTIVE KWAK: NO, ABSOLUTELY NOT,
WHY DO YOU NEED THAT MUCH CASH?

202
00:11:19,471 --> 00:11:21,723
WHAT IF THIS AFFECTS THE COMPANY?
WHY AREN'T YOU ANSWERING?

203
00:11:23,725 --> 00:11:25,394
Then get me 300 million won.

204
00:11:25,477 --> 00:11:27,187
Understood.

205
00:11:29,523 --> 00:11:30,899
How did it go?

206
00:11:33,777 --> 00:11:37,739
How could you actually take all our cash
without discussing it with me?

207
00:11:38,699 --> 00:11:41,577
I hear gold prices are up lately.

208
00:11:41,660 --> 00:11:43,787
How much would we get for our gold bars?

209
00:11:44,788 --> 00:11:47,457
I was told we'd get around 90 million won.

210
00:11:48,876 --> 00:11:51,712
You said you could cover it
with the company money, though!

211
00:11:51,795 --> 00:11:53,172
Now we have to sell the gold too?

212
00:11:53,255 --> 00:11:54,423
I know.

213
00:11:54,506 --> 00:11:57,092
Who knew I'd only be able to withdraw
300 million won?

214
00:11:57,176 --> 00:11:58,760
How can a bank be out of cash?

215
00:11:59,344 --> 00:12:02,639
I was going to withdraw more cash
somewhere else,

216
00:12:02,723 --> 00:12:04,933
but Ms. Kwak was adamant

217
00:12:05,017 --> 00:12:08,729
that withdrawing too much cash in one day
was a serious red flag.

218
00:12:08,812 --> 00:12:10,022
So...

219
00:12:10,105 --> 00:12:12,566
we have 300 million from me,
90 million from the gold bars.

220
00:12:12,649 --> 00:12:14,484
We need around 110 million more.

221
00:12:15,277 --> 00:12:16,737
Do you think you can

222
00:12:17,196 --> 00:12:19,656
<i>get about 100 million won from anywhere?</i>

223
00:12:19,740 --> 00:12:21,783
<i>I'll try to get it too,</i>

224
00:12:21,867 --> 00:12:24,036
<i>but I have a meeting with Michelle now.</i>

225
00:12:25,829 --> 00:12:27,080
Okay, then.

226
00:12:34,004 --> 00:12:37,090
How am I supposed to get
100 million won in a few hours?

227
00:12:40,177 --> 00:12:41,428
Of course.

228
00:12:41,887 --> 00:12:44,681
I'm married too, so I understand.

229
00:12:49,019 --> 00:12:52,397
I have another call.
I'll call you back later, okay?

230
00:12:54,024 --> 00:12:55,150
- Hey.
- <i>It's me.</i>

231
00:12:55,234 --> 00:12:57,361
<i>- </i>How did it go?
- <i>I can get you some money.</i>

232
00:12:57,444 --> 00:12:59,404
- Really?
- <i>Yes, but not too much.</i>

233
00:13:00,280 --> 00:13:02,074
- How much?
- <i>One million won.</i>

234
00:13:02,950 --> 00:13:04,034
<i>That's not enough, is it?</i>

235
00:13:05,452 --> 00:13:06,286
One million won?

236
00:13:06,370 --> 00:13:08,622
<i>Raising a child takes a lot of money.</i>

237
00:13:08,705 --> 00:13:12,626
Right. And considering the economy,
a million won is a lot anyway.

238
00:13:12,709 --> 00:13:13,836
Thank you.

239
00:13:13,919 --> 00:13:15,546
<i>I'm sorry I couldn't help more.</i>

240
00:13:15,629 --> 00:13:19,842
No, don't be sorry.
I'm the one borrowing money from you.

241
00:13:19,925 --> 00:13:21,635
<i>All right.</i>
<i>Let's get a drink some day, okay?</i>

242
00:13:22,678 --> 00:13:25,097
I'll send you
my bank account details then.

243
00:13:26,306 --> 00:13:28,892
- Thanks again.
- <i>I'll send it to your account right away.</i>

244
00:13:30,936 --> 00:13:33,605
MIN-U

245
00:13:34,398 --> 00:13:35,315
So, can you?

246
00:13:36,275 --> 00:13:37,526
About 100 million won.

247
00:13:40,028 --> 00:13:41,196
Right.

248
00:13:43,282 --> 00:13:44,616
Yes, I know it's sudden.

249
00:13:46,118 --> 00:13:48,328
Of course I understand.

250
00:13:48,412 --> 00:13:50,080
I'm sorry to ask you so suddenly.

251
00:13:50,163 --> 00:13:52,583
- Oh, hello.
- Hello, Madam Chairwoman.

252
00:13:53,667 --> 00:13:56,253
- It's been a while.
- Yes, it has. What brings you here?

253
00:13:56,336 --> 00:13:58,922
I have a meeting.

254
00:14:00,007 --> 00:14:01,049
No, it's fine.

255
00:14:01,717 --> 00:14:03,719
- I hope you're doing well.
- I am.

256
00:14:03,802 --> 00:14:06,680
- Good luck with your business.
- Thank you so much.

257
00:14:07,639 --> 00:14:09,850
I'll buy you a meal next time.

258
00:14:10,392 --> 00:14:12,060
Good luck with your meeting.

259
00:14:15,439 --> 00:14:16,273
Okay.

260
00:14:24,114 --> 00:14:24,990
Captain Park?

261
00:14:26,575 --> 00:14:28,160
Aren't you the DIY YouTuber?

262
00:14:29,369 --> 00:14:30,996
I'm such a big fan.

263
00:14:32,706 --> 00:14:34,166
Wow.

264
00:14:34,249 --> 00:14:38,462
You look even more amazing in real life.

265
00:14:38,545 --> 00:14:40,547
- It's nice to meet you.
- You too.

266
00:14:40,631 --> 00:14:42,257
- I've actually been
- I have to--

267
00:14:42,341 --> 00:14:44,885
looking to hire
an interior remodeling company,

268
00:14:44,968 --> 00:14:47,221
and then I just run right into you.

269
00:14:47,304 --> 00:14:48,805
- What a coincidence.
- I actually have to go--

270
00:14:48,889 --> 00:14:51,683
My clinic hasn't opened yet,
so I don't have a business card.

271
00:14:51,767 --> 00:14:53,894
Well, I have one.

272
00:14:54,353 --> 00:14:55,521
- Thank you.
- Call us.

273
00:14:55,604 --> 00:14:57,105
- Can I really?
- Of course.

274
00:14:57,189 --> 00:14:58,857
- My name is Joo Bo-sung.
- Okay.

275
00:14:58,941 --> 00:14:59,983
Bye.

276
00:15:08,450 --> 00:15:09,701
Are you on drugs?

277
00:15:10,494 --> 00:15:11,745
What?

278
00:15:11,828 --> 00:15:13,956
Or is it a woman problem?

279
00:15:14,039 --> 00:15:16,792
You don't strike me
as a sexual predator, though.

280
00:15:19,086 --> 00:15:20,921
Or have you been scammed?

281
00:15:21,004 --> 00:15:22,881
Or maybe you scammed someone.

282
00:15:24,633 --> 00:15:26,385
- Be careful.
- Wait a minute!

283
00:15:27,719 --> 00:15:29,263
Oh, my hips.

284
00:15:29,346 --> 00:15:31,640
What's wrong with you today?

285
00:15:31,723 --> 00:15:34,059
Is that really what you think of me?

286
00:15:35,227 --> 00:15:37,729
Why else would you need
that much money all of a sudden?

287
00:15:37,813 --> 00:15:40,607
And what's with the weird amount?
A hundred and nine million?

288
00:15:42,734 --> 00:15:44,570
Well, you know.

289
00:15:44,653 --> 00:15:46,405
It's complicated.

290
00:15:48,699 --> 00:15:50,284
Fine, I'll lend it to you.

291
00:15:50,367 --> 00:15:51,785
But only because it's you.

292
00:15:53,078 --> 00:15:53,912
Really?

293
00:15:54,705 --> 00:15:55,831
Seriously?

294
00:15:55,914 --> 00:15:58,041
Thank you so much!

295
00:15:58,125 --> 00:15:59,293
You're the best!

296
00:15:59,376 --> 00:16:00,460
Yeah, whatever.

297
00:16:04,006 --> 00:16:06,008
I can't do the whole amount, though.

298
00:16:06,091 --> 00:16:09,011
But I'll still help you out
with some of it, okay?

299
00:16:09,845 --> 00:16:10,888
Okay.

300
00:16:10,971 --> 00:16:13,432
I know times are tough,
so thank you anyway.

301
00:16:14,683 --> 00:16:15,517
By the way,

302
00:16:16,560 --> 00:16:18,187
how much are you thinking?

303
00:16:18,270 --> 00:16:19,980
KIM MIN-U HAS SENT 10 MILLION WON

304
00:16:20,063 --> 00:16:21,815
Is he kidding me?

305
00:16:22,691 --> 00:16:24,610
Only ten million won?

306
00:16:28,071 --> 00:16:31,491
He's always at hostess bars
bragging about his crypto gains.

307
00:16:37,789 --> 00:16:40,751
CONTACTS

308
00:16:40,834 --> 00:16:42,878
MIN-SEO'S MOTHER

309
00:16:46,423 --> 00:16:49,384
